{"school":{"dbn":"32K562","name":"Evergreen Middle School for Urban Exploration","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"32","district_label":"District 32","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":354,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"125 COVERT STREET, BROOKLYN, NY 11207","phone":null,"website":"www.ems562.com","directory_url":null,"accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"On behalf of the entire Evergreen Middle School for Urban Exploration community, thank you for your interest in our school. We are delighted to share our school community with you, and our website is a great place to explore all that Evergreen offers.  We are a vibrant community committed to nurturing independent and creative thinkers, self-advocates, risk-takers, urban explorers, inventors, and leaders through authentic learning experiences. We work collaboratively with families and the community to foster the growth of our children - academically, socially, emotionally, and cognitively. Inside and outside of our classrooms, we offer our students countless opportunities to discover more about the world and about themselves. We proudly celebrate the diversity of perspectives, experiences, and talents represented throughout our community, which fosters joyful collaboration and exploration here every day. As you learn more about who we are, what we do, and what we value at Evergreen, we're here to answer any questions along the way.  Please don't hesitate to contact us! We look forward to getting to know you and are thrilled to partner with you along this journey.    Evergreen Middle School is committed to ensuring that students are able to compete with their peers from across the city. Students have the opportunity to benefit from the following programs: The Middle school Quality Initiative (MSQI). MSQI supports us in developing school wide cross content literacy practices; Edible Schoolyard (through a farm-to-table experiential education model, our students learn how to grow and cook sustainable, organic food. Students and parents grow and cultivate a beautiful garden, and kitchen classrooms enable them to cook the food that they grow); EMS is exceptionally proud to have been a Showcase Schools host for the 2018-2019 school year; We maintain a partnership with the NYC Department of Education's Office of Teacher Recruitment through which our teachers and students help prepare student teachers to enter the classroom.  In order to ensure all students are college and career ready, we offer: Computer Science for All, Civics for All, College Access for All, Algebra Regents, Living Environment Regents, One-to-one laptops.  In addition, Evergreen concluded the 2020-21 school year with a 95% student attendance rate, the highest in District 32.","start_time":"8:15am","end_time":"2:35pm","languages":null,"subway":"J to Halsey St; L to Wilson Av; Z to Chauncey St","bus":"B20, B26, B60, B7, Q24","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":"Bushwick","latitude":40.688922,"longitude":-73.910333,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.967],"st":["ok"],"n":[222.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.949,0.953,0.977,0.936,0.949,0.954,0.959],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"],"n":[389.0,388.0,377.0,388.0,386.0,380.0,374.0],"c":[null,null,null,null,null,1.0,0.901]},"attendance_remote_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.978],"st":["ok"],"n":[375.0]},"chronic_absent_ems_all":{"y":["2015-16","2016-17","2017-18","2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.852,0.888,0.861,0.862,0.877,0.946,0.818,0.877,0.882,0.907],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"],"n":[311.0,338.0,361.0,383.0,382.0,371.0,369.0,374.0,373.0,365.0],"c":[0.714,0.708,0.71,0.743,null,null,null,0.679,0.863,0.703],"s":[4.67,4.99,4.9